; Since dune language 3.21 the dev profile compiles with the compiler's
; default warnings, which leave unused values, opens and fields unreported.
; Keep dune's stricter development set.
;
; A C warning is an error in every profile but release, which must not break
; on a warning a future compiler adds.
;
; The sanitize profile, run on Linux, builds the C under AddressSanitizer and
; UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. rig's env adds the debug runtime and a stressed
; collector, which check a heap so often that suites holding large heaps, such
; as lz's, outran their time. A domain's thread
; exits on the signal stack the OCaml runtime allocated, which
; AddressSanitizer would unmap as its own (use_sigaltstack=0). A refused
; allocation returns NULL as libc's does (allocator_may_return_null=1). CUDA
; and NV map GPU addresses below 2^40, in the shadow gap
; (protect_shadow_gap=0).
;
; The tsan profile, which dune-workspace.tsan sets with a compiler built for
; ThreadSanitizer, compiles the C with the flags that compiler builds its own
; runtime with, so a race through a stub is reported as one through OCaml is.
; A lock-order inversion is reported with both acquisitions' stacks
; (second_deadlock_stack=1). A child forked from a process running threads
; may start threads of its own, as rig's pool does (die_after_fork=0). A
; refused allocation returns NULL as libc's does (allocator_may_return_null=1).
;
; Since dune 3.24 mdx's generator links with the profile's link_flags, so a
; sanitizer's runtime reaches it and sanitized C can link into it. An mdx
; stanza whose libraries hold C is still off under sanitize and tsan: no run
; has shown it passes there on Linux.
;
; An odoc warning is an error in every profile.
;
; WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT bounds each test that sets no ~timeout, so a hung test
; cannot block a shared watch server. Under tsan it is 15 times longer,
; ThreadSanitizer's slowdown at most, and RIG_TEST_TIME_SCALE makes rig's
; suites scale their own timeouts as much.
;
; CACHEDB and XDG_CACHE_HOME put tolk's disk cache, and the files tolk caches
; beside it, in a directory cache of each action's working directory, inside
; _build: a test run reads no entry a user's run wrote and writes none to the
; user's cache.

(env
 (dev
  (flags
   (:standard %{dune-warnings}))
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror))
  (odoc
   (warnings fatal))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)
   (CACHEDB cache)
   (XDG_CACHE_HOME cache)))
 (release
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra))
  (odoc
   (warnings fatal))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)
   (CACHEDB cache)
   (XDG_CACHE_HOME cache)))
 (sanitize
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror
    -g
    -fno-omit-frame-pointer
    -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (link_flags
   (:standard -cclib -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (env-vars
   (ASAN_OPTIONS
    halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0:use_sigaltstack=0:allocator_may_return_null=1:protect_shadow_gap=0)
   (UBSAN_OPTIONS halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1)
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)
   (CACHEDB cache)
   (XDG_CACHE_HOME cache))
  (odoc
   (warnings fatal)))
 (tsan
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror
    -g
    -fno-omit-frame-pointer
    %{ocaml-config:ocamlopt_cflags}))
  (env-vars
   (TSAN_OPTIONS
    second_deadlock_stack=1:die_after_fork=0:allocator_may_return_null=1)
   (RIG_TEST_TIME_SCALE 15)
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 900)
   (CACHEDB cache)
   (XDG_CACHE_HOME cache))
  (odoc
   (warnings fatal)))
 (_
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror))
  (odoc
   (warnings fatal))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)
   (CACHEDB cache)
   (XDG_CACHE_HOME cache))))
